gpio: the sysfs interface's prompt without EXPERT

W19P's libdile_gpio reads and drives its pins through /sys/class/gpio (export, then gpio<N>'s
direction and value), which rtk.ko serves with a fixed-base chip. GPIO_SYSFS has a prompt only
under EXPERT, and EXPERT changes far more than it shows: NAMESPACES and DEBUG_MEMORY_INIT default
off under it (webos-start needs the pid/uts/ipc namespaces) and it selects DEBUG_KERNEL, with
FTRACE, DEBUG_MISC and RCU_TRACE defaulting on. Showing this one prompt changes nothing else.

--- a/drivers/gpio/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpio/Kconfig
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@
 	  that are most common when setting up new platforms or boards.
 
 config GPIO_SYSFS
-	bool "/sys/class/gpio/... (sysfs interface)" if EXPERT
+	bool "/sys/class/gpio/... (sysfs interface)"
 	depends on SYSFS
 	select GPIO_CDEV # We need to encourage the new ABI
 	help
